00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:02.470 align:start position:0%
 
hi there  day 86 except we're gonna actually the  last day is going to be  april the 15th which is next tuesday  so today being thursday friday saturday  sunday monday tuesday i have five days  um  i'm going to meet all my goals except  for writing which i kind of put off  as i've said almost intending not to do  so and then i was pressured to doing so  and i'm glad today i wrote  250 words which i submitted for  correction on our exchange at link  got the uh correction back right away  from one of our korean  native speaking members  um it was great to see the corrections  um it's really it's good you know it  helps me focus it helps me notice  when i'm writing and it takes me a while  to to write 250 words you know i almost  i have the feeling that i wish i were  reading and learning new words and and  doing the things that i most enjoy doing  but  you know i realize that this writing has  got me focusing better i'm more aware of  like some of these sounds in korean  you could use  several symbols for the o sound or for  the a sound and so you start to notice  which ones are used you start to notice  how the words are grouped together  bunched together  so and i think this improves my reading  and proves my comprehension  so the writing  i see the writing and even to some  extent speaking  more as a tool to help me notice so that  that i get more out of my listening and  reading  because to me and i know i was on some  exchange somewhere and somebody was  saying that or on someone's blog that  they were so happy because within two or  three weeks of learning chinese they  were able to put full sentences together  uh i have no interest in being able to  put full sentences together after two or  three weeks doesn't concern me at all  um  my task in learning a language the sort  of basic building blocks blocks to me  are are the words and the phrases i have  to get them in me  whether i can  put phrases together correctly  incorrectly initially uh you know often  in korean they'll teach you the  different polite forms  and you know the names of the different  relationships older brother younger  sister and i have no interest in that at  all to me that is all periphery that's  all kind of decoration the basic  building blocks that i want is is words  uh and lots of words and to get used to  them so that then i can listen to  interesting content like i'm listening  to right now and continue to enjoy the  language consume the language and let  the language grow in me and then at some  point i'll start putting full sentences  together now that i start writing i'm  putting full sentences together i'm  making mistakes spelling mistakes and  mistakes of structure but i am putting  full sentences together and talking  about rather complicated subjects now  that i start writing  so uh however so you know and given that  again i'm  i wouldn't say i'm a dilettante but i do  what i like to do so i mostly listen and  read and but being sort of nudged into  writing uh i wouldn't want to spend too  much time on it but it's it's true like  today i wrote 250 words i hope i don't  think i'll be able to but i'm going to  try to write 250 words for the next five  days i don't think i will but i might  write another thousand words so i've  written a total of about 670 so far so i  might get to say 1500 words which is  half of the goals uh the goal that i had  set for myself i now regret that i  didn't start earlier on the writing i  think it would have helped me it would  have taken time away from my reading and  listening but it would have helped me to  notice help me in other ways  so that you know i'm glad i'm doing it  uh  but as i say  the the main task for me in language  learning is the words because  later on you can always learn about the  names of  relationships or  or you know different levels of  formality  but to understand  you know  substance substantive content you need  words and you need a lot of exposure and  so as i often say i mean that's where i  spend most of my time but  because as i you know attitude got to be  motivated interested confident  time you got to spend the time and you  have to you know develop the ability to  notice and there's no question that  writing seeing the writing corrected  speaking as we do at least seeing the  speaking corrected when it comes back to  you as a report all of that helps you to  notice so that you actually derive more  benefit than when you do your listening  and reading  so  uh  just kind of to this i also had a  discussion today for half an hour with  clara uh in paris  and i'm gonna speak to her at least once  more possibly twice more and then  probably record it as as my sort of  final  uh video in this 90-day challenge but i  have my kim jong-un podcast i have  enough there to keep me going  uh i you know it's so rewarding now i  can read through his podcast and there's  not that many words now that you know a  lot of the yellow words now i've come to  know them and there's fewer and fewer  blue words  uh and many of the blue words are just  forms of words that i already know so as  i've said before i'm over the hump i'm  on my way and if i if i  basically go through all of kim  jung-ha's podcasts uh  you know i'll i'll fix up the the  decoration you know the the fine points  of the  politeness levels and all of that  at the end  i'm not too concerned about it now so  that's basically my report for today  and uh  we're almost at the end here not the end  of my korean studies but the end of the  90 day challenge

